# What the TUI needs to present and run this industry. Engine code does not change per industry.
INDUSTRY|Logistics
PROCESS|Shipment Exception
DEFINITION|definitions/shipment_exception.txt
ABOUT|A delayed or damaged shipment is logged and classified using the courier's tracking system. A coordinator assesses the impact and either reroutes it through the carrier or holds it at the warehouse. The customer is then notified and the case is closed.
EXPECTED|A closed case with the shipment rerouted or held and the customer told. An unknown waybill or an unserved hub makes the external call fail and the task escalates.
PARTICIPANT|log-clerk|Bongani Dube|WarehouseClerk
PARTICIPANT|log-analyst|Kagiso Molefe|ExceptionAnalyst
PARTICIPANT|log-coordinator|Fatima Patel|LogisticsCoordinator
PARTICIPANT|log-dispatch|Pieter Venter|Dispatcher
PARTICIPANT|log-supervisor|Grace Mokoena|WarehouseSupervisor
PARTICIPANT|log-service|Zanele Nkosi|CustomerService
INPUT|waybill|Waybill (WB1001 in transit, WB1002 delayed, WB1003 damaged; others fail)|WB1002
INPUT|destinationHub|New hub (Johannesburg, Durban, Cape Town or Gqeberha; others fail)|Cape Town
OUTCOMES|ASSESS|reroute,hold
